=== P3c steering-scale calibration ROUND 2, written before running: clamped steering (the shifted state is clamped to [-1, 1]); same P3b nets 2400, 2402-2405, point 3600, all arms; scales 0.5, 1, 2.
Why: round 1 (round1/run.log; unclamped addition, scales 1, 2, 4) broke the agent at every scale: unsteered clear abstention 0.5-0.95 against about 0.00 in a plain evaluation, and it grew with the scale (the steering leaked into the following unsteered trials); accuracy on steered trials about 0.5. The agents' state is saturated (most units near +-1) and the look probe flips a block of units (displacement norm about 3), so unclamped addition carried the state far outside the GRU's range.
Selection rule (fixed before any round-2 result), PFATE, medians over the five nets:
  (a) |symmetric random-direction effect| <= 0.05 on A and on C;
  (b) lowest correct-given-report on steered clear trials, over all steering runs, >= 0.9 on A and on C;
  (c) |leak| <= 0.02 on A and on C, where leak = unsteered clear abstention in the steering runs minus a plain evaluation's.
Take the largest scale meeting (a), (b) and (c); if none, the largest meeting (a) and (c); if none, the largest meeting (c); if none, stop and revisit the design.
The summary stays blind: no directional, cross or direction-geometry measure is computed or printed.
